# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Only server/ and web/ are copied into the image, so this file is a second
# line of defence rather than the primary one. It matters most for the two
# risks a COPY alone does not address: build context size, and the chance of
# sweeping a key or a local database into an image.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Secrets. Nothing matching these may ever enter an image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.keystore
secrets.json
mnemonic.txt
privatekey*
**/deployer-key*

# Local databases. A developer's pads.db must never ship and then be mounted
# over — or worse, be served from the image when the volume fails to mount.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# The contracts toolchain is build- and test-time only. Its node_modules is by
# far the largest thing in the repository and none of it is used at runtime.
contracts/

# Test and proof artefacts.
server/test/
web/e2e/
*.png

# Repository and tooling.
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
*.md

# Deployment files themselves do not belong inside the image.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
fly.toml
